 "what_this_is": "Approximate values read off the printed marks BY EYE, recorded so the gallery in png/verify.py can be judged against something other than itself. They were hardcoded in that file, which made the comparison unauditable: a reader whose output drifted could be made to agree by editing the numbers it is compared with, in the same file, in the same commit. Here they are data, and test_visual_verification.py pins this file's SHA-256 - so changing a truth value and changing the declared hash are one diff a reviewer can see.",
 "what_this_is_not": "NOT an attestation and NOT a confirmation. Nobody has signed these and no reviewer identity is recorded; they are one person's approximate reading to about half a printed unit, which is why the tolerances they are used with are stated beside them rather than inferred. A run that agrees with this file is reproducible, not correct.",
