 "segmentation_gold_what_this_is": "The boxes, spines and tick ladders the proposer cut on two hash-pinned clips, recorded so a change to them is a failing scenario. The scenarios before this section asserted only the panel COUNT and that every panel read a ladder - and the proposer CHOOSES its segmentation mode by matching the count a person made, so that assertion is not independent of the thing it checks. An earlier harness run had the count and the ladders unchanged while a box moved and took a third bar group out of the panel: exactly the regression a count cannot see.",
 "segmentation_gold_tolerances": {
  "boundary_px": 2,
  "spine_px": 2,
  "box_iou": 0.98,
  "why": "the clip is pinned by SHA-256 so the cut is deterministic and exact equality would pass today - but a deliberate improvement to the segmenter should be reviewable as a small residual rather than arriving as a wall of unequal integers. A boundary that moves more than two pixels is a different panel."
 },
